## Summary

Fixed the duplicate-membership error Ian encountered when removing himself from Outdoor Movie Night: Dogman. The root cause was a stale guest snapshot racing an invitation-open insert. Client-side lookups and waiting for the local open write proved insufficient for other sessions, private invitation copies, and ordinary-user permissions.

Before: guest removal could race invitation opens, fail with duplicate memberships, or leave someone on the list through an invitation copy or rule.
Now: signed-in and outside-token removal share transactional membership handling; opened-only inserts reuse the current membership and preserve the first-open timestamp. RSVP clearing and membership removal commit together, including for outside invitees without ordinary event visibility.

Before: retaining departures could prevent remove/re-add and ticket purchases, while deleting a retained departure could bypass restoration checks.
Now: voluntary event/party departures use the existing cancelled state, manager exclusions use excluded, and both stay off effective membership, invitation lists and previews. Authorized additions and ticket purchases reuse retained memberships under current joining, payment, eligibility and capacity rules. Ordinary users cannot delete retained departures or downgrade or restore manager exclusions; excluded guests need a list manager to restore them.

Activity invitation exclusions remain separate from volunteer commitments; active volunteers cancel in HCA-Team. No stored columns or enum values were introduced. Regression coverage includes transaction orderings, first-open preservation, ordinary self/household/bringer permissions, outside RSVP removal, restoration and payment rollback, manager exclusions, capacity checks across batches, and consistency across effective membership and previews. Related Go suites, vet, JavaScript syntax checks and diff checks passed; the latest review was clean.

